    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "想 / 要 + verb: want to",
      "body": "To say you want to do something, put 想 or 要 right before the verb. 想 is softer, like 'would like to'. 要 is firmer, like 'want to' or 'going to'. To say you don't want to do something, use 不想. 要 can also go straight before a thing: 我要茶 means 'I want tea.'",
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "我想喝水。",
          "en": "I'd like to drink some water."
        },
        {
          "zh": "你要吃什么？",
          "en": "What do you want to eat?"
        },
        {
